@startuml raditrack_activity_ris_sync
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155

title RADiTrack — Activity Diagram: RIS Sync Agent (Read-Only SQL Server View)

' ==============================================================================
' SWIMLANES
' ==============================================================================

|Hospital IT|
start
:Create view **raditrack.vw_exams**\n(accession, modality, patient class,\nstudy / completed / signed times,\nstatus, last_updated);
:Create login with SELECT\non that view only;
:Share connection details privately;

|RIS Sync Agent|
:Save settings in .env\non a PC inside the hospital network;
:Run **--check**\n(connect read-only, count rows,\nverify columns, validate a sample);
:Start **--watch** (every 5 minutes);

repeat
  |RIS Sync Agent|
  if (Test data loaded in RADiTrack?) then (yes)
    :Skip this round;
  else (no)
    |RIS SQL Server|
    :Return rows with last_updated after\nthe saved position − 10 minutes\n(first run: about 14 months back);

    |RIS Sync Agent|
    while (More rows?) is (yes)
      :Take the next batch (2,000 rows);
      :Map RIS codes to RADiTrack\n(DX/CR → X-ray, MG → Mammogram,\nMR → MRI; O/I/E → OPD/IN/ER);
      :Validate rows; log and skip invalid ones;

      |RADiTrack Database|
      :Look up existing exams\nby accession number;

      |RIS Sync Agent|
      :Plan changes: add new, update changed\n(signed later, category corrected,\ncancelled, sign-off removed), skip unchanged;

      |RADiTrack Database|
      :Apply the batch in one transaction;
      :Calculate TAT and SLA breach\nfor signed reports;
    endwhile (no)

    |RIS Sync Agent|
    :Save the newest last_updated\nas the new position;
    :Log added / updated / unchanged / skipped;
  endif
  :Wait 5 minutes;
repeat while (Agent still running?) is (yes)
->no (Ctrl+C);
stop

@enduml
